WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:18.178
A few hours before the mayor's banquet, Tom was still struggling to remove the prince's helmet.

2
00:00:18.198 --> 00:00:22.622
"Perhaps I should call for help," he thought.

3
00:00:23.803 --> 00:00:25.825
But then he remembered the nuts from lunch.

4
00:00:27.266 --> 00:00:29.608
He wanted to eat them without anyone watching him.

5
00:00:30.804 --> 00:00:35.246
Tom took off the armored gloves, hoping that would make it easier to remove the helmet.

6
00:00:36.586 --> 00:00:38.027
But the helmet didn't budge.

7
00:00:38.047 --> 00:00:41.889
"Ugh!" he shouted in frustration.

8
00:00:43.469 --> 00:00:45.250
Immediately someone knocked on the door.

9
00:00:47.471 --> 00:00:49.852
A servant spoke but did not enter the room.

10
00:00:51.272 --> 00:00:55.514
"I know you don't want to be disturbed this afternoon, but do you need any help?"

11
00:00:57.495 --> 00:00:58.775
"No! Go away!"

12
00:00:59.216 --> 00:00:59.996
Tom shouted.

13
00:01:01.108 --> 00:01:03.409
He pulled on the helmet, but it was still stuck.

14
00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:07.791
Finally he tucked in his chin and gave a mighty tug.

15
00:01:09.092 --> 00:01:11.773
The helmet popped off and hit the floor with a crash.

16
00:01:14.334 --> 00:01:15.675
There was another knock at the door.

17
00:01:15.695 --> 00:01:19.457
"Excuse me, sir," the same servant said.

18
00:01:19.477 --> 00:01:21.478
"Are you all right?"

19
00:01:21.498 --> 00:01:24.379
"I'm fine!"

20
00:01:24.739 --> 00:01:25.460
Tom shouted.

21
00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:31.222
In his dreams about being a prince, he had never had to deal with nosy servants!

22
00:01:33.783 --> 00:01:36.204
At last he settled down on the floor with the nuts.

23
00:01:37.645 --> 00:01:40.206
The heavy metal disk made a perfect nutcracker.

24
00:01:44.728 --> 00:01:49.630
When he finished eating, he put the disk back where he found it—inside an armored glove.

25
00:01:53.712 --> 00:01:58.667
That night Tom was aboard the royal barge with Princess Elizabeth and Lady Jane.

26
00:02:01.589 --> 00:02:06.132
As they sailed down the river toward City Hall, he was amazed by the sights and sounds.

27
00:02:07.873 --> 00:02:12.596
Bonfires burned on both riverbanks, and fireworks boomed overhead.

28
00:02:16.239 --> 00:02:18.200
never seen anything like this!"

29
00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:19.561
Tom blurted out.

30
00:02:19.581 --> 00:02:23.404
"And it sounds like people are cheering for the prince.

31
00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:25.821
I mean, me!"

32
00:02:28.363 --> 00:02:30.966
Princess Elizabeth and Lady Jane looked at each other.

33
00:02:30.986 --> 00:02:36.891
"This isn't the first time people have cheered for him," Lady Jane whispered.

34
00:02:36.911 --> 00:02:39.414
"Why doesn't he know that?"

35
00:02:43.277 --> 00:02:44.699
Princess Elizabeth shrugged.

36
00:02:44.719 --> 00:02:49.263
"But remember, we're supposed to act like nothing's wrong with him."

37
00:02:53.012 --> 00:02:55.813
The banquet took place in a special room in City Hall.

38
00:02:55.833 --> 00:03:03.915
At the sound of a horn, a servant paraded a large piece of meat around the head table.

39
00:03:09.437 --> 00:03:11.517
The mayor and Tom both made toasts.

40
00:03:14.578 --> 00:03:17.999
"Excellent toast, Your Highness," Lord Hertford whispered.

41
00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:20.800
Tom smiled.

42
00:03:22.284 --> 00:03:26.987
"That etiquette book has already come in handy," he thought as he sat down to enjoy the meal.

43
00:03:29.148 --> 00:03:32.570
Dinner was followed by entertainment, which continued for hours.

44
00:03:35.472 --> 00:03:38.854
Sometime after midnight Tom was busy watching a juggler.

45
00:03:43.036 --> 00:03:48.660
At that moment Edward arrived outside City Hall and demanded to be let into the banquet.

46
00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:53.680
"I'm Prince Edward, and this banquet is in my honor!"

47
00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:54.961
he said to the guard.

48
00:03:54.981 --> 00:04:01.767
"Well, I'm a guard, and my job is to keep paupers outside.

49
00:04:02.828 --> 00:04:05.330
Prince Edward arrived hours ago."

50
00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:08.933
"I knew it!"

51
00:04:09.313 --> 00:04:09.994
Edward said.

52
00:04:10.014 --> 00:04:16.420
"That imposter has been wearing my clothes all day, and now he thinks he's the real prince!"

53
00:04:18.856 --> 00:04:20.698
Several people gathered around Edward.

54
00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:27.664
Amused by his accusations, they were hoping to prod him into saying more outrageous things.

55
00:04:27.684 --> 00:04:33.008
"Go home," the guard said to Edward.

56
00:04:33.029 --> 00:04:42.076
"I can see that I don't have any friends here," Edward said, "but I'm not backing down.

57
00:04:42.957 --> 00:04:46.040
When that imposter comes outside, I'll confront him."

58
00:04:47.144 --> 00:04:50.005
A tall, muscular man appeared next to Edward.

59
00:04:51.225 --> 00:04:55.026
His clothes were made of expensive fabric that was now faded and worn.

60
00:04:56.287 --> 00:04:57.867
A rusty sheath held his sword.

61
00:04:59.287 --> 00:05:01.248
He looked almost as poor as Edward did.

62
00:05:01.268 --> 00:05:04.929
"I admire your courage," the man said.

63
00:05:04.949 --> 00:05:09.610
"My name is Miles Hendon, and I'll be your friend."

64
00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:15.832
"Judging by this fellow's clothes, he's another prince in disguise!"

65
00:05:16.264 --> 00:05:17.945
said a man who was watching the scene.

66
00:05:17.965 --> 00:05:21.026
"Let's throw them both in the river!"

67
00:05:22.046 --> 00:05:25.387
But before anyone could grab them, someone arrived on horseback.

68
00:05:25.407 --> 00:05:29.068
"Make way for the king's messenger!"

69
00:05:29.408 --> 00:05:30.248
the rider shouted.

70
00:05:32.509 --> 00:05:36.050
Miles took advantage of the opportunity to scoop up Edward and flee.

71
00:05:38.811 --> 00:05:41.992
The messenger strode into the banquet hall and blasted his horn.

72
00:05:44.264 --> 00:05:47.106
"A message from the palace," he announced.

73
00:05:47.126 --> 00:05:49.967
"The king is dead!"

74
00:05:53.289 --> 00:05:54.630
The guests bowed their heads.

75
00:05:55.771 --> 00:06:01.794
Then they fell to their knees and stretched out their hands toward Tom.

76
00:06:03.115 --> 00:06:07.857
The whole building seemed to shake as they cried, "Long live the king!"

77
00:06:08.898 --> 00:06:12.180
Tom gulped as he took in this astonishing spectacle.

78
00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:17.823
For a moment he didn't know what to say, but finally something occurred to him.

79
00:06:19.044 --> 00:06:20.805
He told the guests to stand.

80
00:06:25.108 --> 00:06:28.651
reign will be one of mercy and peace," Tom said.

81
00:06:28.671 --> 00:06:34.215
"As my first official act, I declare that the Duke of Norfolk will not die."

82
00:06:35.616 --> 00:06:37.217
Tom turned to Lord Hertford.

83
00:06:37.237 --> 00:06:41.460
"I never understood why my father sentenced him to death."

84
00:06:43.484 --> 00:06:45.607
"Long live King Edward!"

85
00:06:46.929 --> 00:06:48.512
The crowd cheered and applauded.

86
00:06:49.773 --> 00:06:53.539
Tom looked out at his loyal subjects and felt his confidence fade.

87
00:06:53.559 --> 00:06:57.264
"How long can I keep fooling all these people?"

88
00:06:57.665 --> 00:06:58.286
he whispered.
